The bounded trace shows the inner circularity works only when its iterable is syntactically `str(CS)`; the tail head loses that static constructor before binding. I’m restructuring the proof around a `Str`-typed identity view:

- define `codesOf(Str)` by the sole `str(CS)` constructor, plus the derived rebuild identity;
- generalize the inner invariant to any `Str` term;
- restate the fixed outer `#iterYield/#loopStep` transition with the guarded identity projection before binding.

